{title: 542 - Jesus, Friend So Kind}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #542 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 542}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus, Friend, [Bb]so kind and [C]gentle,
[Dm]Little [Bb]ones [C7]we bring to Thee:
[Dm]Grant to [Bb]them Thy [C/E]dearest [D7/Gb]blessing,
[Gm]Let [Am/E]Thine arms around [Dm]them be;
[C]Now enfold [Dm]them in [Gm]Thy goodness,
[C7]From all danger keep them free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Thou who did [Bb]receive the [C]children
[Dm]To [Bb]Thyself [C7]so tenderly,
[Dm]Give to [Bb]all who [C/E]teach and [D7/Gb]guide [Gm/D]them
[Gm]Wisdom [Am/E]and humility.
[C]Vision true [Dm]to keep [Gm]them noble,
[C7]Love to serve them faithfully.
{end_of_verse}
